#
# ABox fixture for the p-value-framing competency question "which properties frame a p-value".
# One fully framed math:PValue carrying each edge that makes P(T >= t | H0) unambiguous: its
# magnitude (math:pValue), the null it is computed under (math:nullHypothesis), the sampling
# distribution of the statistic under that null (math:nullDistribution), the statistic driving
# it (math:testStatistic), the tail it is measured over (math:tailDefinition), its enumerated
# math:Sidedness (math:alternativeSidedness, here the lawful individual math:twoSidedAlternative),
# and its multiplicity handling — the adjustment applied (math:pValueAdjustment) over a
# comparison family (math:multipleComparisonFamily). The reasoning-free query projects each
# predicate on the p-value. Unioned onto the merged ontology by gmeow:cqDataFile.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:pval a math:PValue ;
    math:pValue ex:magnitude ;
    math:nullHypothesis ex:null ;
    math:nullDistribution ex:nullDist ;
    math:testStatistic ex:stat ;
    math:tailDefinition ex:tail ;
    math:alternativeSidedness math:twoSidedAlternative ;
    math:pValueAdjustment ex:adjustment ;
    math:multipleComparisonFamily ex:family .
